<mujoco model="panda single cube pickcam">
  <!--
    Camera-enabled variant of mujoco_playground's mjx_single_cube.xml (the model
    behind PandaPickCube / PandaPickCubeOrientation).

    Everything the joint-space task depends on is identical to upstream:
      * <include file="mjx_scene.xml"/> and <include file="sensor.xml"/>
      * body "box" at pos 0.5 0 0.03, same freejoint / geom size / friction /
        condim / contype / conaffinity / solref
      * body "mocap_target"
      * keyframes home / pickup / pickup1 (qpos + ctrl byte-identical)
    so _post_init(obj_name='box', keyframe='home') works unchanged,
    _init_obj_pos == (0.7, 0, 0.03), the 4 contact sensors, nq/nv/nu and the
    observation layout are unchanged, and 200 mj_step's from `home` give qpos
    identical to upstream to 0.0 (verified).

    Added, and nothing else:
      1. camera "front" -- re-aimed at the *PandaPickCube* workspace. pick.py
         resets the box to U(-0.2,0.2)^2 + _init_obj_pos, i.e.
         x in [0.5, 0.9], y in [-0.2, 0.2], z = 0.03, and the mocap target to
         x in [0.5, 0.9], y in [-0.2, 0.2], z in [0.23, 0.43].
         Upstream mjx_single_cube_camera.xml aims at x ~ 1.0 (its box body sits
         at 1.0 and it uses the `low_home` keyframe) and clips this workspace.
         Pose = look-at from (1.35, 0, 0.68) toward (0.60, 0, 0.16); 34.7 deg
         elevation, fovy chosen so the cube region, the gripper's reachable box
         and the floating mocap target all stay inside ~92% of the frame.
      2. geom "workspace_mat" -- a visual-only dark slab over the (white, and
         untextured once use_textures=False) groundplane so the red cube has
         contrast. contype=0 conaffinity=0 => zero dynamics/contact/sensor
         effect; it only exists for the renderer. Sized 10x10 m so it fills the
         whole camera frustum (otherwise the bare white groundplane shows up as
         a saturated band across the top ~15% of the image).
      3. box geom rgba 0 1 0 1 -> 1 0 0 1 (red).

    NOTE ON LOADING: this file lives outside the playground xmls/ directory, so
    its relative includes only resolve through the assets dict:
        from mujoco_playground._src.manipulation.franka_emika_panda import panda
        mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(path.read_text(), assets=panda.get_assets())
    (get_assets() keys mjx_scene.xml / sensor.xml / mjx_panda.xml / meshes by
    bare filename). mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_path() will NOT work.

    CAVEAT: the MJWarp rasterizer ignores geom alpha, so the mocap_target geom
    (rgba "1 0 0 0.2") renders as an OPAQUE box in the same red as the cube.
    See nexus_continuous/scripts/panda_pickcam_probe.py --ghost-rgba.
  -->
  <include file="mjx_scene.xml"/>

  <worldbody>
    <camera name="front" fovy="54" pos="1.35 0 0.68" xyaxes="0 1 0 -0.569780 0 0.821798"/>
    <geom name="workspace_mat" type="box" size="5 5 0.0005" pos="0 0 0.0008"
     rgba="0.10 0.13 0.20 1" contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="0"/>

    <body name="box" pos="0.5 0 0.03">
      <freejoint/>
      <geom type="box" name="box" size="0.02 0.02 0.03" condim="3"
       friction="1 .03 .003" rgba="1 0 0 1" contype="2" conaffinity="1" solref="0.01 1"/>
    </body>
    <body mocap="true" name="mocap_target">
      <geom type="box" size="0.02 0.02 0.03" rgba="1 0 0 0.2" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <include file="sensor.xml"/>

  <keyframe>
    <key name="home"
      qpos="0 0.3 0 -1.57079 0 2.0 -0.7853 0.04 0.04 0.7 0 0.03 1 0 0 0"
      ctrl="0 0.3 0 -1.57079 0 2.0 -0.7853 0.04"/>
    <key name="pickup"
      qpos="0.2897 0.50732 -0.140016 -2.176 -0.0310497 2.51592 -0.49251 0.04 0.0399982 0.511684 0.0645413 0.0298665 0.665781 2.76848e-17 -2.27527e-17 -0.746147"
      ctrl="0.2897 0.423 -0.144392 -2.13105 -0.0291743 2.52586 -0.492492 0.04"/>
    <key name="pickup1"
      qpos='0.2897 0.496673 -0.142836 -2.14746 -0.0295746 2.52378 -0.492496 0.04 0.0399988 0.529553 0.0731702 0.0299388 0.94209 8.84613e-06 -4.97524e-06 -0.335361'
      ctrl="0.2897 0.458 -0.144392 -2.13105 -0.0291743 2.52586 -0.492492 0.04"/>
  </keyframe>
</mujoco>
